(6617964, 986925, 108580, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by RianBotes:</b></div><hr/><i>...i could not shoot this at a better time of the day</i></td></tr></table> <br/>Unless of course the "sun" in the dome is a flash catchlight burst :) Then I understand you completely...It would ''appear'' that this is the case, the low light feeding through the airbrick  window looks late afternoon golden and it has made a relief of the green outer plaster lumps/inconsistencies top left/top right, however it''s created by the ring of flourescent tubes that you cleverly avoided photographing. I actually like the texture it''s created there Rian. It''s nice to know a place and visualise the photographers thinking and positioning.</td>', 'Originally posted by RianBotes:...i could not shoot this at a better time of the day Unless of course the "sun" in the dome is a flash catchlight burst :) Then I understand you completely...It would ''appear'' that this is the case, the low light feeding through the airbrick  window looks late afternoon golden and it has made a relief of the green outer plaster lumps/inconsistencies top left/top right, however it''s created by the ring of flourescent tubes that you cleverly avoided photographing. I actually like the texture it''s created there Rian. It''s nice to know a place and visualise the photographers thinking and positioning.', '2011-12-14 02:59:49.000000', NULL, 0),
